Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Takes Blaze 3.x PS3 clients from "can't connect" to fully authenticated:

- Ps3LoginHandler: accept locally-minted RPCN tickets whose short (~20min)
  TTL already lapsed while the player idled at the "connect to EA" menu —
  expiry is meaningless on our own RPCN, so log it and still verify the
  signature. (Ticket signature itself verifies via the host RPCN key set in
  settings.json HostTicketKey — our self-hosted rpcn uses its own keypair,
  not the official one hardcoded in RpcnSigningKey.)
- Blaze3LoginResponse: the 3.x login response shape heat2 clients require
  (top-level SKEY/NTOS, SESS{1CON,BUID,KEY,UID,PDTL{PLAT,STAS}}), distinct
  from the 2.x Ps3LoginResponse NBA Jam uses; sent only for heat2 clients.
- Push UserSessions UserAdded + ExtendedDataUpdate after login for heat2
  (3.x clients block in login until the server sends the local session).

Verified live: NHL 15 completes SSLv3 TLS -> getServerInstance -> preAuth ->
all config sections -> ps3Login, and the server logs "User uscltest has
signed in". Remaining: the post-login session notification needs the full
3.x UserSessionExtendedData body (ADDR union, QDAT, USER group, ULST) before
the client will send postAuth instead of logging out; reference structures
captured from grid-leak/blaze + open-ds2-server.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
